wered; ~80 series needed for p<0.05). Low AVOID-share bin 52.6% vs 25-50% bin 37.0%.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Series n=50 p=0.07; still confounded by team quality (OKC disciplined and good).", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=50 series; stated need ~80 for p<0.05", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "inconclusive"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:confounding"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:CONFOUNDING"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-058: Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "score": 0.455, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-051 (0.72); FAM:SF-APPA-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-051"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Each star's top sequential suppressor is stable across seasons, and some teammate X->Y sequences have large negative premiums.", "observed_result": "2/30 (7%) stable (>=75% same top suppressor): D. Mitchell PUTBACK 75%, L. James POST_UP 75%. Negative: J. Tatum->K. Porzingis DRIVE->SPOT_UP -0.444 n=31; Giannis->Lillard DRIVE->PNR -0.263 n=31; J. Brown->J. Tatum SPOT_U [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Only 2/30 stars meet the 75% same-top-suppressor stability rule.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars x 4 seasons; min n=20/cell", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-023", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-023: System BEST vs constrained league mix (non-CUT matchup-specificity test)", "score": 0.365, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-024 (0.73); FAM:SF-APPS-023 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-024"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "System BEST vs constrained league mix (non-CUT matchup-specificity test)", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Matchup-specific (non-CUT) BEST counters beat a feasibility-weighted league mix that ignores game state.", "observed_result": "All BEST vs mix: 1.481 vs 1.212, gap=+0.269, p=0.0000, n=283. Non-CUT BEST vs mix: 1.216 vs 1.206, gap=+0.010, p=0.1709, n=136. L3_MATCHUP non-CUT: gap=+0.001, p=0.3277, n=47. BEST vs AVOID gap=+0.692, p=0.0000, n=169. 1 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Key non-CUT test gap=+0.010, p=0.1709, n=136; H2H L3 non-CUT gap=+0.001, p=0.3277. Headline A vs B is CUT-driven.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=136 non-CUT; n=47 L3 non-CUT"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}], "n_results": 10}

